The probability of arrival at the screen site $m$ is therefore $\begin{aligned}
P_m &= |\psi_m+\phi_m|^2 \\
    &= |\psi_m|^2 + |\phi_m|^2 + \psi_m^*\phi_m + \phi_m^*\psi_m.\end{aligned}$ The first two terms are what classical reasoning would have produced. The last two are the interference terms.

